function deepSections(p){
  const details=topicDetails[p.primary]||topicDetails['roll-in showers'];
  const blocks=[];
  angles.forEach(([head,base],i)=>{
    const a=details[i%details.length], b=details[(i+1)%details.length], c=details[(i+2)%details.length];
    const visual = [2,5,8].includes(i) ? `<a class="content-visual" href="/${products[(i*2)%products.length].slug}/"><img src="${products[(i*2)%products.length].img}" alt="${esc(products[(i*2)%products.length].title)} product example" loading="lazy" width="920" height="620"><span>See this ${esc(products[(i*2)%products.length].kind.toLowerCase())} and planning notes →</span></a>` : '';
    blocks.push(`<section class="content-section ${i%2?'tint':''}"><div class="wrap article-grid"><div class="section-no">${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</div><div><h2>${head}: ${titleCase(a)}</h2><p>${base}</p>${visual}<p>For this ${p.primary} decision, focus specifically on <strong>${a}</strong>. Ask what must be true before work begins, what can be verified during installation, and what the owner should receive at completion. Then connect that answer to ${b}. A choice that works in isolation can create a conflict elsewhere—for example, a comfortable seat can narrow an approach, or an attractive enclosure can obstruct caregiver access.</p><p>Use a simple three-column worksheet: “known,” “verify,” and “decide.” Place field measurements and documented product specifications under known. Put concealed framing, plumbing condition, jurisdictional requirements, and manufacturer clarifications under verify. Put finish, accessories, scheduling, and optional upgrades under decide. This prevents preferences from being mistaken for facts.</p><div class="callout"><b>Project checkpoint</b><p>Before approving ${a}, identify who owns the decision, which document controls it, and how it affects ${b} and ${c}. If the answer lives only in a sales conversation, add it to the written scope.</p></div><h3>Questions worth asking</h3><ul class="checks"><li>What field condition could change the plan for ${a}?</li><li>Which current drawing or manufacturer document confirms ${b}?</li><li>How will the installer test or demonstrate ${c}?</li><li>What maintenance or replacement access will remain after finishes are complete?</li></ul></div></div></section>`);
  });
  return blocks.join('');
}

